{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>כוס</b> (cup) — According to Rabbi Moses [ibn Tibbon]: it is like 'my portion and my lot' and 'my cup.' Now the cup is an accident, and it is the bearer. Others said: it is as it sounds." "<b>אשא</b> (I will lift) — like ארים (I will raise). The meaning: because of abundant joy. And he said: 'if distress and sorrow, in the name of HaShem I call.'" "<b>ואם כוס ישועות</b> (and if a cup of salvations) — so as to establish his first statement, for all his days he calls in the name of HaShem, whether in straits or in broad [places]."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 116, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:51.869759944Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}